{"text": "There was a man here named Jim Smiley in the winter of 1849, or maybe the spring of 1850, Wheeler began. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Smiley was the strangest man I ever saw, because he would bet on anything that came up. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> If he could not find anyone to bet on the other side, he would gladly change sides. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> He was lucky, too, so lucky that he almost always came out the winner. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> He bet on horse races and dog fights, and even on which of two birds on a fence would fly first. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> If he saw a bug start to go somewhere, he would bet on how long it would take to get there. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Once Parson Walkers wife was very sick, and for a long time it seemed that nobody could save her. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> When the parson said she was much better, Smiley answered without thinking, Well, I will bet two and a half dollars she does not get well. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Smiley also had a slow, sickly old mare, but he used to win money on her all the same. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Falling far behind at the start, she would get excited near the end and win by a neck.", "alignment": {"characters": ["T", "h", "e", "r", "e", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "a", " ", "m", "a", "n", " ", "h", "e", "r", "e", " ", "n", "a", "m", "e", "d", " ", "J", "i", "m", " ", "S", "m", "i", "l", "e", "y", " ", "i", "n", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "w", "i", "n", "t", "e", "r", " ", "o", "f", " ", "1", "8", "4", "9", ",", " ", "o", "r", " ", "m", "a", "y", "b", "e", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "p", "r", "i", "n", "g", " ", "o", "f", " ", "1", "8", "5", "0", ",", " ", "W", "h", "e", "e", "l", "e", "r", " ", "b", "e", "g", "a", "n", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "S", "m", "i", "l", "e", "y", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "t", "r", "a", "n", "g", "e", "s", "t", " ", "m", "a", "n", " ", "I", " ", "e"